      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A clean look is all about consistency, which is the key to taming the chaos! If you're finding the details overwhelming, try to commit to one citation style and stick to it religiously, even if it feels like a minor rule change. When you're writing, it's often easier to manage the mess by using a reference manager—tools like Zotero or Mendeley can handle the formatting for you, so you don't have to manually worry about whether to use \"et al.\" or list every single name. This way, you focus on your argument, and the software handles the tiny, irritating details.",
      "source": "target",
